      {
        "name": "auth",
        "description": "Credentials: report their health (and store them, if this CLI has any).",
        "commands": [
          {
            "name": "status",
            "description": "Report every provider's credential: where it comes from and whether it works. Never prints values.\n\nWithout --check only presence is reported (status `unchecked` or `missing`).\nExits 0 when every required provider is ok/unchecked (an optional one may be\nmissing), 3 when any required provider has a problem or any credential is\ninvalid/expired, 2 on a usage error. A per-target provider (one credential per\nsite/host/account) gets one entry per stored target, named `<kind>:<target>`. The --json shape is a cross-tool contract:\n`tool`, `version`, `checked_at`, `credentials[]` with `provider`, `required`,\n`fields`, `source`, `source_ref`, `status`, `expires_at`, `quota`, `message`.\n\nExample: textcheck auth status --check --json",
            "options": [
              {
                "name": "--check",
                "description": "Also make one cheap read-only call per provider (10 s timeout) to prove each works.",
                "metadata": [
                  {
                    "name": "x-rb-type",
                    "value": "boolean"
                  },
                  {
                    "name": "x-rb-default",
                    "value": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "name": "--provider",
                "arguments": [
                  {
                    "name": "PROVIDER",
                    "required": true
                  }
                ],
                "description": "Report only this provider, or one target as <kind>:<target> (default: all).",
                "metadata": [
                  {
                    "name": "x-rb-type",
                    "value": "str"
                  }
                ]
              },
